The three starts specifically cover:

- **Size-first:** preserves capacity for large models and avoids fragmentation.
- **Pressure-first:** spreads latency-sensitive/high-request models early.
- **Pressure-density-first:** accounts for pressure generated per GB consumed.

All candidates still use the same strictly improving relocation and swap operations, so the returned placement remains memory-feasible and never worsens the selected construction’s maximum KVPR.
